## What a `type: human-actor` instance is

**A human actor memorial describes a human collaborator** at the identity level.  The same human running in multiple runtime contexts (unsandboxed vs sandboxed, different hosts, different authorization scopes) is **one actor instance** with multi-arity `runs-in-context:` edges to the contexts they operate in.

Human Actor is a subtype of [`actor`](actor.md) → [`meta`](meta.md).

## Identity-and-context orthogonality

The ContextL-style orthogonality pattern: one human identity + multi-arity context edges, not one-per-context actor instances.  This is the same pattern as `:in-layer` dispatch in ContextL — identity is stable; context is the orthogonal dispatch axis.

Authorization / firewall rules dispatch on the `(actor-identity, active-context)` tuple — not on per-context actor instances.

