## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Human Actor memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` (and `actor`) plus human-specific slots:

- **`runs-in-context`** (required) — rel-paths to context memorials (multi-arity for humans operating in multiple contexts)
- **`belongs-to`** — organization rel-paths (employers / projects / collaborations)
- **`role`** — named role tag (director / contributor / reviewer / etc.)

{{slot-table}}

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## Who this person is

<Role, primary engagement with the corpus, distinguishing
collaboration characteristics.>

## Operating contexts

<Which contexts this person operates in (cross-reference context
memorials).>

## Authorizations + standing directives

<Cross-reference authorization memorials granted by this person.>

## Voice / discipline signature

<If applicable: characteristic phrases, naming conventions,
quality standards this person enforces.>

## See also

<Adjacent actors, governing authorizations, applicable rules.>
```

## Composition with adjacent classes

- **`organization`** — humans typically `belongs-to` employer / project organizations
- **`context`** — humans run in contexts; multi-arity `runs-in-context:` captures all
- **`authorization`** — authorizations granted BY a human typically reference the granting actor
- **`feedback`** / **`preference`** / **`decision`** — these guidance memorials often have a `created-by:` or `directive-from:` edge to a human actor

